>>strangulation (you'll surely know this one when you wear it!)
>>change  (changes your alignment)
  (No, you're thinking about a helm of opposite alignment.  This 
   amulet changes your sex).
>>ESP (lets you see monsters behind walls if you are close enough,
>>	and gives you telepathy)
>>life saving (saves you from death once and gets destroyed in the process)
>>magical breathing (lets you walk under water)
>>amulet vs. poison (you are poison resistant while wearing it)

>Cursed amulet of restful sleep comes to mind. Urrrrrrrgh. (you just fall asleep
>one day and never wake up >=)

Plus amulet of reflection.

>moral: given (roughly) a 2 of 8 chance that your amulet is a *bad* thing
>(25%)...*never* put one on blindly. (unless you are desperate, i.e. about
>to *die*. =)

Real moral: Find out if the amulet is cursed.  If it's uncursed/blessed
then always put it on.  (As soon as there are no real nasties around).
   - Amulets of strangulation you take off right away.
   - Aumlets of restful sleep you take off after the first time you fall
     asleep.
   Amulets of change are then about the worst thing that can happen to
   you.  The rest are all potentially good.  I'd hate to get killed
   while carrying an Amulet of Life saving.
